[ti:Hotel California (cover)]
[01:48.40]On a dark desert highway, cool wind in my hair
[01:54.44]Warm smell of colitas, rising up through the air
[02:00.88]Up ahead in the distance, I saw a shimmering light
[02:06.98]My head grew heavy and my sight grew dim
[02:10.26]I had to stop for the night
[02:13.48]There she stood in the doorway;
[02:16.65]I heard the mission bell
[02:20.26]And I was thinking to myself,
[02:22.22]'This could be Heaven or this could be Hell'
[02:26.32]Then she lit up a candle  and she showed me the way
[02:32.72]There were voices down the corridor,
[02:35.92]I thought I heard them say...
[02:39.31]Welcome to the Hotel California
[02:44.68]Such a lovely place
[02:46.39]Such a lovely  face
[02:51.59]Plenty of room at the Hotel California
[02:59.35]Any time of year, you can find it here
[03:04.42]Her mind is Tiffany-twisted, she got the Mercedes bends
[03:10.93]She got a lot of pretty, pretty boys, that she calls friends
[03:17.58]How they dance in the courtyard, sweet summer sweat.
[03:23.82]Some dance to remember, some dance to forget
[03:30.24]So I called up the Captain,
[03:33.28]'Please bring me my wine'
[03:35.74]He said,'We haven't had that spirit here since  nineteen sixty nine'
[03:43.31]And still those voices are calling from far away,
[03:49.59]Wake you up in the middle of the night
[03:52.90]Just to hear them say...
[03:56.10]Welcome to the Hotel California
[04:01.61]Such a lovely place
[04:03.36]Such a lovely  face
[04:08.29]They livin' it up at the Hotel California
[04:16.14]What a nice surprise, bring your alibis
[04:21.52]Mirrors on the ceiling,
[04:24.48]The pink champagne on ice
[04:26.60]And she said 'We are all just prisoners here, of our own device'
[04:34.02]And in the master's chambers,
[04:37.04]They gathered for the feast
[04:40.34]The stab it with their steely knives,
[04:43.12]But they just can't kill the beast
[04:47.05]Last thing I remember, I was
[04:50.40]Running for the door
[04:53.87]I had to find the passage back
[04:56.14]To the place I was before
[05:00.28]'Relax,'said the night man,
[05:02.64]We are  programmed to receive.
[05:06.52]You can checkout any time you like,
[05:09.55]but you can never leave!
